sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Client / User Thread (10,000 Concurrent)
    participant Gateway as API Gateway (Envoy)
    participant VWR as Virtual Waiting Room
    participant InvSvc as Inventory Service
    participant Redis as Redis Cluster ({product_1001})
    participant DB as PostgreSQL (Durable Store)
    participant Kafka as Kafka Event Bus

    User->>Gateway: POST /api/v1/reservations (Idempotency-Key: UUID)
    Gateway->>Gateway: Check IP/User Rate Limit (Token Bucket)
    Gateway->>VWR: Validate Admission Token
    VWR-->>Gateway: Token Valid
    Gateway->>InvSvc: Forward Reservation Request
    
    InvSvc->>Redis: EVALSHA reserve_inventory.lua (stock_key, res_hash, idem_key)
    
    alt Stock Available (First 100 Reqs)
        Redis->>Redis: DECRBY stock_key 1 (Stock > 0)
        Redis->>Redis: HSET res_hash idem_key payload (RESERVED)
        Redis-->>InvSvc: Return SUCCESS (Reservation ID: res_9981)
        InvSvc-->>Gateway: HTTP 201 Created { reservation_id, status: "RESERVED" }
        Gateway-->>User: HTTP 201 Created
        
        InvSvc->>DB: Async Write Local Outbox Event (RESERVATION_CREATED)
        InvSvc->>Kafka: Outbox Poller Publishes `salestorm.reservation.created`
    else Stock Depleted (Remaining 9,900 Reqs)
        Redis-->>InvSvc: Return SOLD_OUT (Stock == 0)
        InvSvc-->>Gateway: HTTP 409 Conflict { error: "SOLD_OUT" }
        Gateway-->>User: HTTP 409 Conflict ("Flash Sale Stock Depleted")
    end
